                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2cee240c-1ae4-3ea1-aed4-838bcf3ec7e4",
                        "entry_id": "e00b6228-28f5-3728-9c78-be26fb7f78bd",
                        "glosses": [
                            "volume (of a book)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "9de1bfc2-f13e-49a8-a6b6-e80f6a167c51",
                                "sense_id": "2cee240c-1ae4-3ea1-aed4-838bcf3ec7e4",
                                "text": "Лео́нтий о́бмер, уви́дя ты́сячи три волю́мов — и ста́рые, запылённые, заплесневе́лые кни́ги получи́ли но́вую жизнь, свет и употребле́ние: пока́, как ви́дно из письма́ Козло́ва, како́й-то Марк чуть бы́ло не доко́нчил де́ла мыше́й.",
                                "translation": "Leonty was horrified at the sight of the condition of the three thousand or so volumes, and he saw to it that the old, dusty, and mildewed books were exposed to the light, put to use, and received a new lease of life; but as we know from Kozlov’s letter, a certain Mark had all but completed the work done by the mice.",
                                "english": "Leonty was horrified at the sight of the condition of the three thousand or so volumes, and he saw to it that the old, dusty, and mildewed books were exposed to the light, put to use, and received a new lease of life; but as we know from Kozlov’s letter, a certain Mark had all but completed the work done by the mice."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
